<span class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Quick Answer</span></div><p class="text-base sm:text-lg font-medium text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100 leading-relaxed mb-0">San Gimignano's ZTL is permit-only and runs 00:00-24:00 daily. Guests of hotels and B&amp;Bs enter free 07:00-09:30; at any other hour the property must pre-register your plate first.</p></div><p class="not-prose my-4 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 border-l-2 border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-600 pl-4">Locally the zone is called <strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Zona a Traffico Limitato San Gimignano</strong> (Italy) &mdash;
that is the wording on the boundary signs, on the official portal and on any penalty notice,
so it is the phrase to search for once you are there.</p><div class="not-prose my-6 rounded-2xl border border-sky-200 dark:border-sky-800/50 bg-sky-50/50 dark:bg-sky-950/20 p-5"><p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-400 mb-3">Next</p><ul class="space-y-2.5 text-sm"><li><a href="/tools/emission-zone-checker/#city=san-gimignano" class="font-medium text-sky-800 dark:text-sky-300 underline">Check your own car against San Gimignano</a>
