<svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentcolor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13 7l5 5m0 0-5 5m5-5H6"/></svg></a></div></div><h2 id=san-gimignano-ztl--zona-a-traffico-limitato>San Gimignano ZTL — Zona a Traffico Limitato</h2><p>The <strong>Zona a Traffico Limitato</strong> in San Gimignano, Italy is a camera-enforced historic-centre zone. Access is granted by permission — for residents and permit-holders — rather than by a vehicle&rsquo;s Euro emission class. A brand-new car with no permit is treated the same as an old one.</p><h3 id=who-can-enter>Who Can Enter?</h3><ul><li><strong>Residents</strong> with a valid ZTL permit, and vehicles on the <em>lista bianca</em></li><li><strong>Guests of hotels, B&amp;Bs and holiday lets</strong> — free 07:00-09:30 without registration; otherwise the property registers your plate on the Polizia Municipale portal</li><li><strong>Guests staying five nights or more</strong> — one extra entry a day outside 07:00-09:30, pre-registered</li><li><strong>Disabled badge holders</strong> — with valid permit</li></ul><h3 id=entering-without-a-permit>Entering Without a Permit</h3><p>Cameras automatically detect unregistered plates. Fines of <strong>EUR 83-332</strong> are sent to your registered address — including foreign-registered vehicles. San Gimignano does not publish its own figure, so this is the national art. 7 Codice della Strada range rather than a local tariff. Rental car fines are charged to your credit card plus an admin fee.</p><h3 id=how-to-get-access>How to Get Access</h3><p>If you arrive between 07:00 and 09:30 you need nothing at all; the disciplinare gives accommodation guests free access in that window. At any other time ask reception to register your plate on the Polizia Municipale portal before you drive up — properties without private parking inside the ZTL are obliged to warn guests and to register them. Between 15:00 and 20:00 that registration only covers the secondary streets, Via del Castello and Piazza Cisterna, and only for dropping off, not parking. Otherwise, use the car parks outside the walls and walk in.</p><h3 id=what-zone-does-it-cover>What Zone Does It Cover?</h3><p>The ZTL covers the walled historic centre, entered through six controlled varchi including Porta San Giovanni, Via di Quercecchio and Porta San Matteo, with a 30 km/h limit inside. Lorries, articulated vehicles and buses are barred outright. The rules above come from the town&rsquo;s own <a href=https://www.comune.sangimignano.si.it/it/documenti_pubblici/ztl-centro-storico-di-san-gimignano>disciplinare for ZTL access authorisations</a>, which states that &ldquo;la ZTL ha validità normalmente tutti i giorni nell&rsquo;orario 0:00/24:00&rdquo;. Never drive past a ZTL sign without a registered plate.</p><section class="changelog my-8 p-5 sm:p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700"><div class="adbox my-8 text-center min-h-[100px] no-print"><div class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-400 dark:text-slate-500 mb-1">Advertisement</div><ins class=adsbygoogle style=display:block data-ad-client=ca-pub-7423435551681993 data-ad-slot=2569874852 data-ad-format=auto data-full-width-responsive=true></ins><script>(adsbygoogle=window.adsbygoogle||[]).push({})</script></div><h2 class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-base sm:text-lg mb-4"><svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentcolor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5H7A2 2 0 005 7v12a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2h-2M9 5a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2M9 5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2m-6 9 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
